                                <li>Shift Start saves each shift as one board ({BOARD_TABLE} while the shift is on, {ARCHIVE_TABLE} once it has ended) with a row for each person and room; the old Shift Start saved one row per person in craa5_taskassignment. Both are read a stretch of days at a time: the boards whose shifts fall in it (the live boards once, for the newest stretch) and the old rows that no board covers, so a shift that has a board is counted from the board alone and nobody counts twice. A new row for the same person ends the one before it.</li>
                                <li><b>Times assigned</b> counts one shift in one area once, even if the person was moved back and forth within it. A night shift (6 PM to 6 AM) counts for the day it began, so the early-morning hours stay with it.</li>
